Room: the context menu of a Room page goes to the host.

Chrome builds a page's context menu as a RenderViewContextMenu (every
IDC_CONTENT_CONTEXT_* command: link, image, media, editing, spellcheck
suggestions, Add to dictionary, Look Up) and shows it with its Cocoa runner
(RenderViewContextMenuMacCocoa). Room shows its own NSMenu with Room's items
first and then the engine's (the Engine protocol's willShowContextMenu, Phase
2.6a), so the host needs the built model and a way to execute one of its
commands.

No existing hook: the menu is built and shown inside
ChromeWebContentsViewDelegateViewsMac, the WebContentsViewDelegate Chrome's
ContentBrowserClient creates for every WebContents at creation (before
RoomCore wraps it); WebContentsDelegate::HandleContextMenu belongs to
Chrome's BrowserWebContentsDelegate. //room takes the built menu (it keeps it
alive until the host selects or cancels) only for pages it wraps whose
delegate presents menus; every other page keeps Chrome's.

Phase 3.4a, 2026-10-05. //room: room/core/room_context_menu.mm.
